/-!
# Root-marked PSL₃ recognition

The six-root elementary presentation recognizes a nontrivial centerless
finite quotient as PSL₃, including fields of orders two and four. For an
actual split rank-two Tits system, positive generation and negative-root
placements identify its unipotent subgroup, entire Borel and both marked
parabolics. Restricting the same equivalence gives the marked amalgam
comparison and literal quotient formulas in either orientation.

Source: Steinberg §6, pp.71–74; DGS, Groups and Graphs, Theorem D, p.224.
-/
